 m south onto its block, its front facing east across Leuvenstraat to the long Waalse Kaai square of the filled-in dock, now lined with plane trees; the houses on the street's north end across from it added. The site was widened to 140 m so the warehouses behind fit. Still guessed: all dimensions and heights, the façade's material and colour, where the tower stands, the inner court's shape (the outlines show an open court in the middle of the block, which the model leaves open). The new M HKA planned by Christ & Gantenbein and Bovenbouw is not shown."}